!! Edges

<<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/lararium-identity >> — the five scales, the vessel key, the delegation edge, the lease, the siege-gate, the lineage fold. This meme expands its axis with //what makes a scale real//; it replaces nothing there.

<<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-circle >> — ''carries two of this meme's claims at a higher register, better grounded.'' //Anon is the base; a known handle is a disclosure act// — with Nissenbaum's contextual integrity behind it, and the sharper reading that staying veiled runs as ''appropriate flow, never a deficit or an un-climbed ladder.'' That states #vocabulary's //participation minus office// with a citation this meme lacks. And its veil-crossing law — the lease decaying linkage back toward the anon floor while a severed past ''does not re-weld'' — states the ONE-WAY RATCHET #rank names from the Roman side (`praescriptio` running //PRO libertate et NON ADVERSUS libertatem//). ''Read persona-circle first on both.''

<<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/group-as-closure >> — ''holds #the-constructor already, and holds it with the declaration built in.'' Its groups form as a ''reciprocal-edge closure'': //each member declares their own signed, typed, `lar:`-named edge//, and the group stands as //the set of edges that mutually name each other//. That is the mutual hold and the declared partition as ONE mechanism rather than two — //groups stand as relational constructs built from distributed name bindings//. ''Read it as the constructor's build; read #the-constructor as what the build implies.''

<<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/identity-classes >> — carries #rank's fluidity from the cost side: //an identity drifts UP the ladder as it accretes value it cannot cheaply re-mint//. Standing rises with what a party would forfeit by refounding, which prices the ladder without ordering anyone against anyone.

